## Rework after the review (two minor fixes)

**Photo window clipped its own ring and shadow (owner-visible while dragging).** `.demo-zone__window`
carried `overflow: hidden`, which clipped the item's `::before` ring and `::after` card shadow: after
the first drag the window lost its 1 px border (also after re-docking) and its border fade/shadow
never rendered, while the notepad kept both. The clipping now lives on a new inner wrapper
(`.demo-zone__window-inner`, which keeps the 32 px title bar, the image and the rounded corners) and
the zone item itself no longer clips, so its ring and shadow render like the notepad's. Verified in
the browser:

```
docked / redocked window: overflow visible, ::before ring opacity 1 (rgba(255,255,255,0.08)),
                          ::after shadow opacity 0 (--card-shadow present, not clipped)
mid-detach (0.50):        ring opacity 0.5, shadow opacity 0.5 (window), same as the notepad
detached (1.00):          ring opacity 0, shadow opacity 1 with the full --card-shadow visible
notepad (unchanged):      ring 1 / 0.5 / 0, shadow 0 / 0.5 / 1 at the same progress values
```

**README wording.** "fades its border in (1 → 0)" now reads "fades its border out (1 → 0)".

