## Interaction check (CDP pointer events, real layout measurements)

Chrome for Testing 156 with CDP device metrics; a temporary out-of-repo helper drove it
(`Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride`, `Page.navigate`, `Page.captureScreenshot`,
`Emulation.setEmulatedMedia`, and real `PointerEvent`/`KeyboardEvent` dispatch inside the page); it
was removed after the run. Screenshots are scrolled so the whole demo surface is visible.

```sh
node /tmp/p028-cdp.mjs "http://127.0.0.1:4200/apps/web/preview/" "reviews/evidence"
```

### Threshold and hysteresis (screen px outside the zone edge, 1440 × 900)

```
pointer outside | state    | data-detach-progress | item x (world)
10 px           | docked   | 0.29                 | 501.2
20 px           | docked   | 0.80                 | 574.3
27 px           | docked   | 1.00                 | 608.1
29 px           | detached | 1.00                 | 610.6   <- detach at 28 px
20 px (back)    | detached | 1.00                 | 601.6   <- hysteresis keeps the state
12 px (back)    | detached | 1.00                 | 593.6
6 px (back)     | docked   | 0.12                 | 515.0   <- dock below 8 px
```

- Detach needs **28 screen px** of pointer travel outside the zone edge; docking again needs at most
  **8 px** (hysteresis band 8–28 px, so a wobble at the edge cannot flicker).
- Release halfway (`ZONE_RELEASE_DISTANCE` 18 px) settles to the nearest state: a mid-detach release
  at 14 px settled back to the docked slot (item back at 447 / 90.5).
- At 50 % progress (14 px outside) the computed style is `matrix(1.01, 0, 0, 1.01, …)`, the border
  overlay opacity is 0.5 and the `--card-shadow` overlay opacity is 0.5.

### Detached, redocked, zoom, cancel, second pointer

```
detached (both items out, free):
  notepad state=detached progress=1.00 transform=(112, 224) scale 1.02 grid-snapped
  window  state=detached progress=1.00 transform=(800,  64) scale 1.02 grid-snapped
  border overlay opacity 0 (faded), --card-shadow overlay opacity 1
  slots stay in the zone card: notepad 240 x 89 at (447, 90.5), window 240 x 140 at (447, 191.5)
redocked:
  both items state=docked progress=0.00, transforms (447, 90.5) and (447, 191.5) — the exact slots
  status: "Image window docked back in the zone."
detached status: "Image window detached — free on the canvas."
zoom 150 % (screen-pixel thresholds):
  14 screen px outside -> progress 0.53 (0.5 in screen px; a world-pixel threshold would read 0.75)
  40 screen px outside -> detached, clamped inside the world (rect 913..1280 on the 1440 viewport)
pointer cancel during a detach drag: settles detached (state=detached, progress 1.00)
second pointer during a notepad drag: ignored — the window stayed docked, only the notepad moved
```

